Hermes patch: Zero's Wallet. Cards and ID numbers fill only with a one-time approval the hub redeems for the exact page.
Base: ~/taffy/hermes at 74943bb889 (Oct 9, 2026). Apply: cd ~/taffy/hermes && git apply ~/taffy/patches/hermes-wallet.patch
Design: docs/plans/2026-10-19-wallet.md (Zero repo).

What it changes:
- agent/vault_store.py: a new `identity` kind (secret `value` plus `id_type` and an optional `issuer`, with an
  origin); address items also hold name, phone and email; `redaction_values(kind, secret)` lists every secret
  field of every kind plus the spaced and dashed groupings of a card or ID number, and the reformattings a
  page gives a phone or a date of birth.
- agent/vault_login_classifier.py: classify_identity_control / select_identity_fill find the one field an ID
  belongs in (license, passport, SSN, date of birth); address fills also map name, tel and email. build_fill_js
  takes top_origin and frame_origins for a fill inside an iframe.
- tools/browser_vault_tool.py: payment and identity fills need `approval`. register_approval_redeemer(fn)
  installs the check (Zero's taffy-tools plugin asks its hub); the fill reads the page's real origin and its
  visible order total, redeems the approval for them, and only then registers redaction and writes the page.
  With no redeemer, every card and ID fill is refused. _confirm_payment_fill (the "vault-payment" elicitation)
  is gone. Address items saved without an origin fill the open address form on that tab's own origin; the
  Zero plugin gate decides when. Every secret field of every kind is registered for redaction.
  register_login_site(fn) installs how to name a host's site (the plugin registers consent.login_site, its Public
  Suffix List rule); a login item then also fills on an https page of the same site as one of its saved origins
  (OpenAI saves at platform.openai.com and asks for the password on auth.openai.com, Oct 20 2026). With no rule
  registered, logins fill only on their exact origins. Cards, IDs and addresses never widen.
  _focus_own_tab sends every fill, code entry and login save to the tab the agent's snapshots and clicks use, when
  that tab holds the form. Before it, two tabs on one login page could put the password in the other tab, and the
  fill said success while the agent's box stayed empty (Oct 30 2026, Bloomerang).
  A checkout whose card fields are in a payment processor's iframe (Stripe Elements on js.stripe.com, the only
  origin in _CARD_FRAME_ORIGINS) gets the card written into that frame. The frame must sit inside the page the
  approval was redeemed for, with only that page's origin and processor origins between them, and its fill script
  checks the same against location.ancestorOrigins: a third party's frame on the checkout can't host a Stripe
  frame that gets the card. Frames are written before the page, and once a frame holds the card a later failed
  write still reports a fill (with a warning), so the plugin keeps the screen lock and the spent approval.
- tools/browser_supervisor.py: child_frames(top_origin, origins) lists the attached page's cross-origin iframes on
  those origins (never another tab's) whose every ancestor frame is on top_origin or those origins, and
  evaluate_in_frame(target, expression) evaluates in one of them.
- hermes_cli/vault.py: `hermes vault add` prompts the identity fields.
- agent/redact.py: registered vault values are scrubbed in any letter case, matched on casefolded text so a "straße"
  the page shows as "STRASSE" goes too.
- tests: the payment test now covers approvals; identity, address, order-total, same-site login and card-iframe tests
  are new, and test_browser_supervisor.py has a real-Chrome test of child_frames and evaluate_in_frame.

